course: dictionary
lesson: 10349
title: Translator
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A translator is a person whose job is to change writing from one language into another. The words around the word give you clues. «Behind many AI news stories stand real people with real worries: translators, artists, writers and parents.» The translators are in a list of people who do jobs, so they are people, not things.
explain: «Puns hardly ever survive translation, because the two meanings live in one language's words; a translator has to invent a new pun instead.» A pun is a joke that plays on words with two meanings. The clues show that a translator has to make a new joke when the old one does not work in another language.
explain: A translator can also be a computer program or app that changes words from one language into another. You may see an «online translator» on a website. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: A translator changes writing from one language into another.
fact: A translator app or online translator is a computer program that changes words from one language into another.
fact: An interpreter is usually the name for a person who changes spoken words on the spot.
fact: Phrases you may meet: «work as a translator», «a translator app», «online translator».
fact: «Translator» can also mean someone who puts something difficult into easier words for others.
exercise: «Behind many AI news stories stand real people with real worries: translators, artists, writers and parents.» What is a translator in this sentence? | *A person who changes writing from one language into another | A parent who reads bedtime stories | A writer of news stories | A computer that makes news stories
exercise: «Puns hardly ever survive translation, because the two meanings live in one language's words; a translator has to invent a new pun instead.» What must a translator do when a pun does not translate? | Ask the reader to guess the joke | *Invent a new pun instead | Leave the joke out and say nothing | Copy the pun word for word
exercise: Dad uses an online translator to read a letter from Spain. What is an online translator? | A teacher who visits schools | *A computer program that changes words from one language into another | A bus that drives across Spain | A map of Spain's hills
test: «It was reported that some translators, writers and artists say they now get less work because of AI.» According to the sentence, why might translators get less work? | Because they stopped reading | *Because of AI | Because they are on holiday | Because the sun is shining
test: Which word means someone who puts something difficult into easier words for others? | *Translator | Astronaut | Giant | Baker
exam: Which of these is the best meaning of translator in «work as a translator»? | A machine that makes sandwiches | A person who sells tickets at a cinema | *A person whose job is to change writing from one language into another | A child who learns to draw
